From: Corios00 <52224974+Corios00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:12:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A hero's own sheathe press plays the sheathe and unsheathe
 clips on every client (patch 0104)

Elwynn Survival's R goes to the server, which changes UNIT_FIELD_BYTES_2 byte 0, and 1.12 adopts
a changed byte with an instant SetSheatheState (0x604c70): the weapons jumped between hand and
back with no movement, for the hero and for everyone watching. Only a Z press (ToggleSheath)
played the Sheath 89 / HipSheath 90 clips.

The server now also counts the hero's presses in byte 1, which 1.12 leaves zero. A sheath byte
that changes together with that count is played as the ceremony, on any unit: the same per-arm
masked stow and draw legs as a Z press, each weapon moving at its arm's $SHR/$SHL key, with the
draw/stow sound. A change that leaves the count (a blow drawing, a meal putting away) still
snaps, and ends a ceremony still playing; so does an add-on's swing taking the body. A model
without both clips, a rider, or a unit first seen snaps as before.

Each arm now takes its own key ($SHR right, $SHL left) where a model keys them apart
(HumanFemale's HipSheath, 0.40 and 0.67 sec), and a new ceremony stops one still playing.
